From 4b7a18179ff39ed061087a19f797203d669f1fca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Tridgell <andrew@tridgell.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:09:51 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] brush-dataset: keep single-channel 16-bit and float
 images as numeric targets

16-bit grayscale (value / 65535) and float images are packed as the f32 bits
of the value instead of being converted to RGBA8, so scalar targets such as
scaled temperature keep their precision and see no gamma. SceneBatch records
the format in float_gt.
